    "english":  "The dried leaves of the black-stemmed mara tree swirl in the dust,\ncarried aloft by the whirlwind across the barren plains.\nIn the scorching noon, when shade itself seems to flee from the sun,\nthe male pigeon calls mournfully to its weary mate upon the parched ridge.\nSeeing their shared devotion in that merciless heat,\nwill not my lover\u0027s heart turn back toward the home he left behind?\nHow can a heart that knows love endure the wilderness,\nwhen memories of my tear-stained face must rise like cool water in his soul?",
